Title: Tell ICU's genccode the CPU architecture by a name it knows
Origin: electron-legacy (this repo)

The 32-bit build reaches ICU's data step and stops there:

  generating object code for ../../deps/icu-tmp/icudt78l.dat
  CPU architecture "ia32" is unknown.
  error MSB8066: Custom build for '..\..\deps\icu-tmp\icudt78l.dat'
  exited with code -1. [.../tools/icu/icudata.vcxproj]

genccode validates its -c argument in pkg_genc.cpp's checkCpuArchitecture,
which accepts x86, x64, arm and arm64 in either case and nothing else. The
icudata target hands it <(target_arch), and GYP's name for 32-bit x86 is ia32:
configure.py renames it on the way in, with the comment that the build tools
prefer ia32 "even if we prefer the latter". Every other consumer of
target_arch is happy with that name; this one tool is not.

So the mapping is done once, as a target-level variable, and used at both
call sites -- the Clang branch and the MSVC one, which pass the same argument
from two different actions.

Only x86 needs it. x64, arm and arm64 are spelled the same on both sides, and
the else branch passes target_arch through unchanged so nothing else moves.

Upstream does not hit this because upstream does not build 32-bit Windows any
more; see 08-restore-32-bit-vcbuild.patch for the gate that stops it earlier.

diff --git a/tools/icu/icu-generic.gyp b/tools/icu/icu-generic.gyp
--- a/tools/icu/icu-generic.gyp
+++ b/tools/icu/icu-generic.gyp
@@ -132,6 +132,23 @@
       'target_name': 'icudata',
       'type': '<(library)',
       'toolsets': [ 'target' ],
+      'variables': {
+        'conditions': [
+          # genccode checks this against x86/x64/arm/arm64 and rejects
+          # anything else outright:
+          #
+          #   CPU architecture "ia32" is unknown.
+          #
+          # ia32 is GYP's name for 32-bit x86 -- configure.py renames it on
+          # the way in, noting that the build tools prefer it over x86 -- so
+          # it has to be mapped back for the one tool that does not know it.
+          [ 'target_arch=="ia32"', {
+            'icu_cpu_arch%': 'x86',
+          }, {
+            'icu_cpu_arch%': '<(target_arch)',
+          } ],
+        ],
+      },
       'conditions': [
         [ 'OS == "win"', {
           'conditions': [
@@ -151,7 +168,7 @@
                       # for Clang use "-c <(target_arch)" option
                       'action': [ '<(PRODUCT_DIR)/genccode<(EXECUTABLE_SUFFIX)',
                                   '<@(icu_asm_opts)', # -o
-                                  '-c', '<(target_arch)',
+                                  '-c', '<(icu_cpu_arch)',
                                   '-d', '<(SHARED_INTERMEDIATE_DIR)',
                                   '-n', 'icudata',
                                   '-e', 'icudt<(icu_ver_major)',
@@ -208,7 +225,7 @@
                   'outputs': [ '<(SHARED_INTERMEDIATE_DIR)/icudt<(icu_ver_major)<(icu_endianness)_dat.<(icu_asm_ext)' ],
                   'action': [ '<(PRODUCT_DIR)/genccode<(EXECUTABLE_SUFFIX)',
                               '<@(icu_asm_opts)', # -o
-                              '-c', '<(target_arch)',
+                              '-c', '<(icu_cpu_arch)',
                               '-d', '<(SHARED_INTERMEDIATE_DIR)/',
                               '-n', 'icudata',
                               '-e', 'icusmdt<(icu_ver_major)',
